WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.039
Wukong and his companions walked through the Western Paradise.

2
00:00:07.040 --> 00:00:12.452
The road weaved through a field of flowers and toward the Spirit Mountain.

3
00:00:12.453 --> 00:00:17.215
Bajie looked up at the huge mountain and shook his head.

4
00:00:17.216 --> 00:00:20.373
"It won't be easy to climb that."

5
00:00:20.374 --> 00:00:22.846
[g@Wukong laughed.

6
00:00:22.847 --> 00:00:26.205
"Don't ask me to carry you!"@g]

7
00:00:26.206 --> 00:00:31.131
The travelers soon arrived at a river with a strong current.

8
00:00:31.132 --> 00:00:37.040
Waves crashed into jagged rocks, spraying water everywhere.

9
00:00:37.041 --> 00:00:40.593
"This river looks dangerous," said Wujing.

10
00:00:40.594 --> 00:00:44.818
"But we must cross it to get to the Spirit Mountain."

11
00:00:44.819 --> 00:00:47.557
[g@Bajie sighed.

12
00:00:47.558 --> 00:00:51.189
"We will never be able to cross this river safely.

13
00:00:51.190 --> 00:00:53.504
Let's just go home."@g]

14
00:00:53.505 --> 00:00:57.582
[g@"Nonsense," said Wukong.

15
00:00:57.583 --> 00:00:59.376
"Look over there."@g]

16
00:00:59.377 --> 00:01:02.101
[g@The monkey pointed upstream.

17
00:01:02.102 --> 00:01:05.656
A thin log lay across the river.@g]

18
00:01:05.657 --> 00:01:10.067
It wobbled and shook as the water rushed under it.

19
00:01:10.068 --> 00:01:12.816
[g@The Tang Monk looked at the log.

20
00:01:12.817 --> 00:01:14.600
"Don't be silly, Wukong.@g]

21
00:01:14.601 --> 00:01:18.453
[g@We can't walk across that log—it's too thin.

22
00:01:18.454 --> 00:01:21.091
And it looks quite slippery."@g]

23
00:01:21.092 --> 00:01:26.657
"But that log is the only way to reach the Spirit Mountain," said Wukong.

24
00:01:26.658 --> 00:01:30.913
"You must believe that it's safe. Watch me!"

25
00:01:30.914 --> 00:01:43.251
The monkey hopped onto the log and ran across the river and back.

26
00:01:43.252 --> 00:01:47.498
"See?" he said. "It's safe."

27
00:01:47.499 --> 00:01:49.869
[g@Bajie snorted.

28
00:01:49.870 --> 00:01:52.310
"You don't weigh much, Wukong.

29
00:01:52.311 --> 00:01:55.910
But if I step on that log, it will break."@g]

30
00:01:55.911 --> 00:01:58.809
[g@"I believe Wukong," said Wujing.

31
00:01:58.810 --> 00:02:02.975
"We must walk across the log."@g]

32
00:02:02.976 --> 00:02:06.165
[g@"Follow me, Master," said Wukong.

33
00:02:06.166 --> 00:02:09.661
He pulled the Tang Monk toward the log.@g]

34
00:02:09.662 --> 00:02:12.233
The monk trembled with fear.

35
00:02:12.234 --> 00:02:14.308
[g@"Don't make me walk across that!

36
00:02:14.309 --> 00:02:17.244
I'll fall into the river and drown!"@g]

37
00:02:17.245 --> 00:02:21.301
"Let's just fly over the river," suggested Bajie.

38
00:02:21.302 --> 00:02:25.027
"We can carry Master and the horse."

39
00:02:25.028 --> 00:02:27.525
"No," insisted Wukong.

40
00:02:27.526 --> 00:02:31.656
"The Tang Monk must make the entire journey by himself.

41
00:02:31.657 --> 00:02:35.040
We're here to protect him, not to carry him.

42
00:02:35.041 --> 00:02:41.366
Buddha won't allow Master to have the True Scriptures if he doesn't take every step himself."

43
00:02:41.367 --> 00:02:46.537
Just then an old man appeared in a boat.

44
00:02:46.538 --> 00:02:50.292
"I can take you across the river," said the man.

45
00:02:50.293 --> 00:02:54.785
[g@"Thank you," said the Tang Monk.

46
00:02:54.786 --> 00:02:57.596
He walked to the riverbank.@g]

47
00:02:57.597 --> 00:03:01.118
[g@"My companion wanted me to walk across that log, but—"

48
00:03:01.118 --> 00:03:03.848
The monk gasped.@g]

49
00:03:03.849 --> 00:03:07.697
"There's something wrong with your boat," he said to the man.

50
00:03:07.698 --> 00:03:09.920
[g@"It has no bottom!

51
00:03:09.921 --> 00:03:12.796
Water is flowing right through it!"@g]

52
00:03:12.797 --> 00:03:15.656
"The boat is safe," said the man.

53
00:03:15.657 --> 00:03:17.155
[g@"Please climb in.

54
00:03:17.156 --> 00:03:19.198
Buddha is waiting."@g]

55
00:03:19.199 --> 00:03:29.836
With a bit more hesitation, the Tang Monk stepped into the boat.

56
00:03:29.837 --> 00:03:33.811
He was shocked to find that he didn't sink.

57
00:03:33.812 --> 00:03:39.480
He sat on the edge of the boat as Wujing led the horse aboard.

58
00:03:39.481 --> 00:03:46.445
Bajie and Wukong followed.

59
00:03:46.446 --> 00:03:51.525
[g@The boat glided swiftly across the river.

60
00:03:51.526 --> 00:03:56.090
Suddenly there was a splash.@g]

61
00:03:56.091 --> 00:04:02.040
The Tang Monk looked at the water and saw a body floating downstream.

62
00:04:02.041 --> 00:04:03.246
[g@He screamed.

63
00:04:03.247 --> 00:04:05.317
"A man has drowned!"@g]

64
00:04:05.318 --> 00:04:09.297
[g@Wukong put his hand on the monk's shoulder and smiled.

65
00:04:09.298 --> 00:04:11.519
"It's you, Master."@g]

66
00:04:11.520 --> 00:04:15.010
"What?" said the monk. "Me?"

67
00:04:15.011 --> 00:04:19.301
"Wukong is right!" cried Bajie. "It [i@is@i] you!"

68
00:04:19.302 --> 00:04:23.460
"Look again, Master," said Wujing, smiling.

69
00:04:23.461 --> 00:04:27.206
The Tang Monk looked at the body more carefully.

70
00:04:27.207 --> 00:04:31.777
It was wearing the same Buddhist robe that he was wearing.

71
00:04:31.778 --> 00:04:35.239
[g@"It [i@is@i] me," said the monk quietly.

72
00:04:35.240 --> 00:04:37.455
"But how . . . ?"@g]

73
00:04:37.456 --> 00:04:41.579
"You got rid of your mortal body, Master," said Wukong.

74
00:04:41.580 --> 00:04:43.945
"You're a spirit now."

75
00:04:43.946 --> 00:04:52.763
"You're one of us!" Bajie beamed.

76
00:04:52.764 --> 00:05:05.687
The boat soon reached the other riverbank, and the travelers stepped out.

77
00:05:05.688 --> 00:05:13.441
As they walked up the slope of the Spirit Mountain, the Tang Monk laughed in amazement.

78
00:05:13.442 --> 00:05:15.844
"I feel so light!" he said.

79
00:05:15.845 --> 00:05:19.255
"I feel like I could run right up this mountain!"

80
00:05:19.256 --> 00:05:23.840
"Good," said Bajie. "Perhaps you could carry me?"

81
00:05:23.841 --> 00:05:33.197
Everybody laughed as they continued up the mountain.

